  (:id "platform-specific"
   :title "Historical preview-1 baseline: platform-specific tests"
   :text ("Preview-1 tests that apply to only some platforms: one row per platform a test applies to. These green cells are not preview-2 qualification." "Windows lifecycle stress registers portable, IOCP and RIO server cells for five 1000-cycle real-loopback cases. Each case warms once, then accounts process handles, SDK resources by generation, threads, RocketNet's HeapCreate-backed allocator and private bytes. RIO registrations and completion/request queue identities are separate. Unknown closes, duplicate live identities and ledger overflow fail. SDK identities must close, threads must not grow, library heap growth is limited to one page per ten minutes with a one-page floor, and private-byte growth stays under one page per cycle. Same-host time is diagnostic only. Run one registered test_<cell>_transport_windows_*_1000 case at a time with ./bin/Release/functional.exe --run on an otherwise idle Windows machine. test_windows_lifecycle_ledger checks balanced generations, raw-value reuse while an old generation closes, bounded-child termination on stale close and reported capacity overflow.")
   :label "test"
   :specific t
   :columns ("Windows" "macOS" "Linux")
   :rows
   ((:feature "UDP connection reset (SIO_UDP_CONNRESET) never stalls receive" :on Windows :cell y :source "functional/windows_connreset.cpp, tests/test_iocp.cpp" :evidence "Windows: landed as 561142df; the test_*_transport_windows_connreset_* cases in functional.exe, green on Windows in landed 4529ca2d")
    (:feature "Application Verifier" :on Windows :cell y :source "the CI workflows" :evidence "Windows: 0 verifier stops, 7457d35b")
    (:feature "App Nap and timer coalescing keep client timing" :on macOS :cell o :source "docs/MACOS.md (the App Nap timing cases are retired)" :evidence "macOS: the App Nap timing cases have been retired" :pending "retired: OS scheduling and process throttling are outside RocketNet's control (docs/MACOS.md)")
    (:feature "MemorySanitizer (msan.yml)" :on Linux :cell y :source ".github/workflows/msan.yml, tools/msan_known.txt" :evidence "Linux: msan.yml run 39514217624 at 330e951e passes")
    (:feature "Big-endian system build and suites" :on Linux :cell p :source ".github/workflows/nightly-bigendian-system.yml, tools/bigendian/" :pending "planned for the final deliverable")
    (:feature "Windows lifecycle stress: portable, IOCP and RIO cells are registered; execution remains unqualified" :on Windows :cell n :source "functional/windows_lifecycle_stress.cpp")
    (:feature "Windows lifecycle stress: five 1000-cycle real-loopback cases cover init/term, endpoint create/destroy, connect/disconnect and restart" :on Windows :cell n :source "functional/windows_lifecycle_stress.cpp")
    (:feature "Windows lifecycle stress: SDK identities are checked separately; process-wide handle deltas are unattributed and not ownership evidence; threads stay flat, heap growth is bounded and same-host time is diagnostic" :on Windows :cell n :source "functional/windows_lifecycle_stress.cpp")
    (:feature "Windows lifecycle ledger: balanced generations, raw-value reuse, stale-close child termination and capacity overflow" :on Windows :cell n :source "functional/windows_lifecycle_stress.cpp")
    (:feature "Live XDP test (an XDP server, a client on every test machine)" :on Linux :cell p :source "docs/LIVE-XDP.md, tla/MCRNLiveFleetRun.cfg" :pending "planned for the final deliverable: after v1.0.0-preview-1")))
  (:id "transports"
   :title "Historical preview-1 baseline: tests per transport"
   :text ("Preview-1 tests that apply to every transport: one row per test, one column per transport, in the order the automatic ladder ranks them. These green cells are not preview-2 qualification." "xdp, gso and io_uring build on Linux, msgx on macOS, iocp and rio on Windows, and portable and loopback on all three; a portable or loopback cell is ✅ only when it is green on all three.")
   :label "test"
