  (:id "release"
   :title "Release-wide test inventory and historical preview-1 results"
   :text ("Tests that are neither per platform nor per transport: model checks, proofs, reviews and checks of the code as a whole. New planned rows inventory post-preview-1 work; old green rows are preview-1 history. Neither qualifies preview-2 without the exact-head receipt in the first table." "The lean CI selection is a rapid per-commit regression signal, not a substitute for full native, platform, nightly, sanitizer, fuzz, model or qualification gates. Linux Release leg a runs each selected exact name once in manifest order without retries; a missing name or first nonzero result stops the step and remains in the Actions log. Its unit runner uses the DEV=0 test target and includes the production-only refusal witness. Its functional runner remains the existing DEV target and supplies portable socket and worker behavior without being production-library evidence. Diagnostic reruns are separate and cannot change the gate result." "The per-commit combined unit and functional execution budget is a CI acceptance rule, not an SDK or runtime performance guarantee. Every build-and-test Linux, macOS and Windows row, XDP functional row, happy-path integration row, backend-example unit row, sanitizer row, big-endian execution row, TSan lifecycle row and pinned-sodium unit row starts a fail-closed monotonic receipt immediately before its first required unit, functional, lifecycle, transport, consumer or integration execution and closes it after its last one, including required checks between them. These jobs have no needs dependencies, so their parallel maximum is the critical path; a future genuinely serial dependency must be added to the path instead of evading the bound. Queue wait and pre-test build or provisioning time are separate. Dedicated fuzz, conformance, platform-selftest and validation-tool jobs retain their distinct required per-commit categories and job bounds rather than being mislabeled as unit or functional intervals. Passing is strictly below 120000 milliseconds, 60000 milliseconds or less is the ideal, and only actually scheduled nightly work is exempt." "The 2026-10-26 exact per-commit receipt found that the exhaustive sanitized functional run was still inside its first invocation after 164 seconds. The per-commit sanitizer functional row therefore keeps exact reconnect-isolation, send-ring recovery and loopback-UDP cases followed by the lifecycle, driver, sodium and XDP-negative controls. The unchanged exhaustive functional suite is owned by nightly-leaks: it is scheduled daily at 06:20 UTC under the same ASan and UBSan flags plus LSan, has a 30-minute bound, and a red run is owned by the next morning's estate. Scheduled run 40283240918 at 02aee1a0 completed the full suite green; that execution proves the nightly owner and oracle, not the current candidate head.")
   :label "test"
   :columns release
   :rows
   ((:feature "Combined required unit and functional CI timing configured, execution unqualified: every per-commit unit, functional, lifecycle, transport, consumer and integration row records one fail-closed monotonic interval; parallel rows qualify by their maximum, passing is below 120000 milliseconds and 60000 milliseconds or less is the ideal" :cells (n) :source ".github/workflows/ci.yml")
    (:feature "Sanitizer cadence configured, current candidate execution unqualified: exact reconnect-isolation, send-ring recovery, loopback-UDP, lifecycle, driver, sodium and XDP controls remain per commit; the unchanged exhaustive functional ASan, UBSan and LSan suite is a daily required release gate in nightly-leaks with next-morning estate ownership" :cells (n) :source ".github/workflows/ci.yml and .github/workflows/nightly-leaks.yml")
    (:feature "Lean CI configured, execution unqualified: configuration resolution and refusal with test_create_reports_status_config_refusals; exact public-create statuses followed by valid create and destroy" :cells (n) :source "tests/test_unit_create_reports_status.cpp")
    (:feature "Lean CI configured, execution unqualified: authenticated token handling with test_token_time_refusals_are_distinct; signed requests refuse expiry and future creation and accept both boundaries" :cells (n) :source "tests/test_unit_token_time_refusals.cpp")
    (:feature "Lean CI configured, execution unqualified: sequence, ACK and replay with test_small_in_order_exactly_once_under_loss_and_reorder; bidirectional ACKs suppress replayed duplicates and drain exactly once" :cells (n) :source "tests/test_unit_channel_ordered.cpp")
    (:feature "Lean CI configured, execution unqualified: reliable ordering and receipts with test_ordered_receipt_after_all_chunks; no receipt precedes every ordered chunk ACK" :cells (n) :source "tests/test_unit_channel_receipts_reliable.cpp")
    (:feature "Lean CI configured, execution unqualified: timeout recovery with test_message_config_never_received_is_reliable_timeout; lost CONFIG from the other side disconnects both endpoints and tears down cleanly" :cells (n) :source "tests/test_unit_message_config.cpp")
    (:feature "Lean CI configured, execution unqualified: resource-exhaustion recovery with test_transport_ring_exhaustion; portable send-ring refusal regains exact capacity and delivers fresh payload before shutdown; the functional target links the DEV library, so this proves portable behavior but not the production library" :cells (n) :source "functional/rocketnet_functional_tests.cpp")
    (:feature "Lean CI configured, execution unqualified: disconnect and reconnect isolation with test_session_reconnect_isolation_portable; three portable socket generations isolate stale traffic through worker shutdown; the functional target links the DEV library, so this proves portable behavior but not the production library" :cells (n) :source "functional/session_reconnect_isolation.cpp")
    (:feature "Lean CI configured, execution unqualified: DEV=0 boundary with test_production_client_refuses_dev_connect_token; development key refusal, production key acceptance and destroy" :cells (n) :source "tests/test_unit_production_refusals.cpp")
    (:feature "Production functional executable (functional_production, ./bin/functional_production): links the production library (rocketnet, ROCKETNET_DEV=OFF), never rocketnet_dev, and is built only in a production build; CI runs it on the Linux, macOS and Windows Release rows through the auto ladder and the portable rung pinned by env, the same two passes as the DEV functional suite, including test_session_reconnect_isolation_portable and test_transport_ring_exhaustion; it runs the portable transport on every OS and each native transport the OS builds (gso and io_uring on Linux, msgx on macOS, iocp and rio on Windows) through test-owned production keys minted with the production token writer" :cells (n) :source "CMakeLists.txt, functional/main.cpp, functional/harness.inc, functional/rocketnet_functional_tests.cpp, .github/workflows/ci.yml" :pending ((status "Configured, execution unqualified at this release: on macOS Release the two named cases and the msgx reconnect-isolation case pass and the unit suite passes with ROCKETNET_DEV ON and OFF; the thread check refuses growth and allows an OS thread to exit, so an OS thread that exits does not stop the production run; Linux and Windows production execution is registered in CI and was not run locally, so CI is the gate there")))
    (:feature "functional_production exclusion list (development scaffolding only, stated in CMakeLists.txt; no case, bound, timeout or assertion in the DEV functional suite is removed or weakened): functional/channel_*.cpp (in-memory network simulator and lossy link), functional/environment_wiring.cpp (development env and simulator), functional/shared_library_tokens.cpp (development-token minting), functional/process_thread_counts.cpp (development server secret), functional/posix_hard_killed_client.cpp (platform test seams), test_client_ipv4_without_ipv6_stack (ipv6 test seam), test_server_handshake_deadline_from_config (internal client protocol test filter), and test_public_client_server_queries, test_public_client_reads_server_disconnected and test_two_address_token_connects_over_ipv4 (published development keys), plus the Linux the DEV send-error seam cases test_gso_client_transport_wire_ipv4, test_gso_client_transport_wire_ipv6, test_gso_client_transport_wire_plain, test_gso_client_transport_wire_gro, test_gso_shutdown_send_interruptions, test_gso_transport_held_receive_view, test_gso_transport_linux_sendmmsg_errors, test_gso_transport_linux_recvmmsg_errors, test_io_uring_transport_linux_receive_cqe_errors, test_io_uring_transport_linux_send_cqe_errors, test_gso_server_refuses_explicit_port_in_use, test_uring_server_refuses_explicit_port_in_use, test_xdp_transport_linux_receive_weather_ipv4 and test_xdp_transport_linux_receive_weather_ipv6, the xdp hard-killed cells test_posix_hard_killed_client_xdp_ipv4_client_portable, test_posix_hard_killed_client_xdp_ipv6_client_portable, test_posix_send_to_closed_port_xdp_ipv4_client_portable, test_posix_send_to_closed_port_xdp_ipv6_client_portable, test_posix_client_server_gone_xdp_ipv4_client_portable and test_posix_client_server_gone_xdp_ipv6_client_portable, test_client_destroy_early_threaded_keeps_then_frees and test_server_destroy_early_threaded_keeps_then_frees (bodies in functional/destroy_early_keep.cpp, not compiled into this executable), and the stall-destroy tail of test_server_uring_probe (rocketnet_server_uring_test_stall_destroy and rocketnet_server_uring_test_resume_stop). The posix thread-count cases are not excluded: they need no development scaffolding, so they stay in functional_production unweakened" :cells (n) :source "CMakeLists.txt and functional/rocketnet_functional_tests.cpp" :pending ((status "The thread check refuses growth and allows an OS thread to exit: test_posix_init_term_1000, test_posix_server_create_destroy_1000 and test_posix_client_create_destroy_1000 pass when the thread count is equal or lower and fail when it grows; descriptors and heap umems stay an exact match; fleet CI status for these cases is unqualified until CI runs them")))
    (:feature "Send budget: packets_per_update 256 at 60 Hz, receive sized at least 2x" :cells (p) :source "tests/test_unit_send_budget.cpp, tla/MCRNSendBudget.cfg" :pending ((status "planned for the final deliverable")))
